Subject: [PATCH 08644/11362] Phase 3a gate: NOT MET, underpowered plus a real
 regression (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6246)

5-game HUD-masked held-out change-fidelity A/B for
CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_PROMPT_ENRICHMENT. Only 4/5 comparable (m0r0's "on" arm
hit a genuine 1575s timeout, not a crash). Of the 4: tr87 improved
substantially (+0.33), cn04 marginally (+0.01), ft09 tied (unmeasurable),
ar25 regressed substantially (-0.67) -- larger in magnitude than tr87's
gain. Gate fails for two independent reasons: short of its own >=5-game
floor, and the available signal is mixed-to-negative regardless (a
hypothetical clean 5th data point could not alone satisfy the gate without
also explaining away ar25's regression).

Caught a real methodology bug in the smoke test before the full run: the
verifier call left HUD masking on its ambient default (silently unmasked)
instead of forcing hud_mask_enabled=True to match Phase 1a's own
measurement convention. Fixed before the real run.

Isolated from the conductor's shared results/arc_e3 engine store via
CARNOT_ARC_E3_DIR pointed at a private scratch directory, avoiding the
known project_arc_engine_store_regression overwrite hazard.

SUBMITTED_INDUCE_PROMPT_ENRICHMENT_ENABLED stays default OFF.

determination_preservation_lint, adversarial_verify, artifact_freshness_lint
all clean.
